## 1. Architectural Changes

### Current Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Frontend<br>React + Ant Design"] -->|POST /api/upload-plan| B["Backend<br>Node.js + Express"]
    B -->|POST /calculate-quantities| C["ML Service<br>FastAPI + PyTorch"]
    C -->|quantities + overlays| B
    B -->|hardcoded rates ⟶ costs| A
    B -->|POST /generate-3d-geometry| C
```

**Current pain points identified in codebase:**
- Rates hardcoded in [config/index.js:33-68](file:///c:/Users/Ridma%20Chalana/Desktop/green-build/backend/config/index.js#L33-L68) — no versioning, no DB
- [costModel.js](file:///c:/Users/Ridma%20Chalana/Desktop/green-build/backend/models/costModel.js) uses static config rates — no material type support
- [uploadController.js](file:///c:/Users/Ridma%20Chalana/Desktop/green-build/backend/controllers/uploadController.js) does detect + cost + respond in one shot — no user confirmation step
- [floorPlanController.js:162-229](file:///c:/Users/Ridma%20Chalana/Desktop/green-build/backend/controllers/floorPlanController.js#L162-L229) generates BOQ in-line with upload — categories limited to walls/doors/windows/flooring
- Frontend [boqModel.js](file:///c:/Users/Ridma%20Chalana/Desktop/green-build/frontend/src/models/boqModel.js) already has 6 sections (from last session) but backend doesn't support them

### Target Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Frontend
        FE1["Step 1: Upload Floor Plan"]
        FE2["Step 2: Review & Edit Detections"]
        FE3["Step 3: Material Selection + Manual Inputs"]
        FE4["Step 4: Confirm → BOQ + 3D"]
    end

    subgraph Backend["Backend (Node.js)"]
        API1["POST /api/upload-plan → ML detect only"]
        API2["POST /api/detections/confirm"]
        API3["GET /api/rates?section=&material="]
        API4["POST /api/rates/upload (Admin CSV)"]
        API5["POST /api/boq/generate"]
        API6["POST /api/generate-3d-geometry"]
        RE["Rate Engine Module"]
        BG["BOQ Generator Module"]
    end

    subgraph Database["MongoDB"]
        DB1["rates (NEW)"]
        DB2["floorplans (MODIFIED)"]
        DB3["boqreports (MODIFIED)"]
    end

    subgraph ML["ML Service (FastAPI)"]
        ML1["/calculate-quantities"]
        ML2["/generate-3d-geometry"]
    end

    FE1 -->|upload image + scale + height| API1
    API1 -->|image| ML1
    ML1 -->|detections JSON| API1
    API1 -->|detections + overlays| FE2
    FE2 -->|confirmed detections + edits| API2
    API2 -->|save to DB| DB2
    FE3 -->|material choices + quantities| API5
    API5 --> RE
    RE --> DB1
    API5 --> BG
    BG --> DB3
    API5 -->|full BOQ JSON| FE4
    FE4 -->|trigger 3D| API6
    API6 --> ML2
```

### Key Architectural Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **New `Rate` model** (not embedded) | Rates are shared across all projects; need history + CSV import |
| **Split upload from BOQ** | Introduces user confirmation step between ML detection and BOQ generation |
| **Rate Engine as service module** | Single source of truth; called by BOQ generator; easily testable |
| **Keep frontend boqModel.js** | Already has 6-section generator from last session; just needs dynamic rates |
| **Backward-compatible API** | Old `/api/upload-plan` still works but response shape changes (returns detections, not costs) |

